## DATABASE SCHEMA

Create these two tables in Supabase:

### Table: sessions
- id: uuid, primary key, default gen_random_uuid()
- participant_name: text, not null
- started_at: timestamp with time zone, default now()
- completed_at: timestamp with time zone, nullable
- score: integer, nullable (server-calculated only)
- total_time_seconds: integer, nullable
- is_complete: boolean, default false
- position: integer, nullable (1, 2, or 3 — updated after each submission)

### Table: answers
- id: uuid, primary key, default gen_random_uuid()
- session_id: uuid, foreign key → sessions.id
- question_number: integer, not null
- question_text: text, not null
- selected_answer: text, nullable (null if timer ran out)
- correct_answer: text, not null
- is_correct: boolean, default false
- answered_at: timestamp with time zone, default now()

### Supabase Row Level Security (RLS)
Enable RLS on both tables.

sessions policies:
- INSERT: allow for anon (participants can create their own session)
- SELECT: allow for authenticated only (admin can read all)
- UPDATE: allow for authenticated only (server updates score/position)

answers policies:
- INSERT: allow for anon (participants can insert answers)
- SELECT: allow for authenticated only (admin can read all)

