## ADMIN DASHBOARD — /admin

### Login Page (/admin/login)
- Simple email + password form
- Uses Supabase Auth (signInWithPassword)
- On success: redirect to /admin/dashboard
- On fail: show "Invalid credentials"
- No public signup — admin account is pre-created in Supabase dashboard

### Route Guard
- /admin/dashboard checks for active Supabase session server-side
- If not authenticated: redirect to /admin/login
- Wrap in middleware.ts using Supabase auth helpers

### Dashboard Page (/admin/dashboard)
- Subscribe to Supabase Realtime on the sessions table
- Auto-updates live as participants complete the quiz
- Show a manual "Refresh" button as fallback

#### SECTION 1: Stats Bar (top of page)
Four stat cards in a row:
- Total Participants (count of all sessions)
- Completed (is_complete = true)
- In Progress (is_complete = false)
- Gold Achievers (score >= 16)

#### SECTION 2: Podium — Top 3 Winners
Visual podium layout (2nd | 1st | 3rd from left to right):

  [2nd Place]      [1st Place]      [3rd Place]
  Silver bg        Gold bg          Bronze bg
  Name             Name             Name
  Score: X/20      Score: X/20      Score: X/20
  Time: Xm Xs      Time: Xm Xs      Time: Xm Xs
  ⭐ Gold Achiever  ⭐ Gold Achiever

- 1st place card is taller/larger (like a real podium)
- ⭐ Gold Achiever badge only shows if score >= 16
- If position slot is empty: show "Waiting..." placeholder card
- Colors: 
  - 1st: #D4AF37 (gold) background
  - 2nd: #C0C0C0 (silver) background  
  - 3rd: #CD7F32 (bronze) background

#### SECTION 3: Full Leaderboard Table
Columns: Rank | Name | Score (/20) | Time | Gold Achiever | Status

- Sorted: score DESC, total_time_seconds ASC
- Top 3 rows: gold / silver / bronze left border or row tint
- Gold Achiever: ⭐ if score >= 16, blank otherwise
- Status: "✅ Completed" or "⏳ In Progress (Q X of 20)"
- For in-progress participants, show current question number if available
- Clicking a row expands the Review section for that participant

#### SECTION 4: Review & Corrections
- Accordion list of all COMPLETED participants
- Click participant name to expand their answer sheet
- For each of the 20 questions show:
  - Question number and text
  - Their answer: highlighted GREEN if correct, RED if wrong
  - Correct answer: always shown in green below their answer
  - "No answer (timed out)" shown in grey if they ran out of time
- This section is used for the live review/correction segment 
  after the quiz where answers are gone through publicly

